@startuml flow-game-loop
!theme plain
skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center

title Game Loop - Automatic Updates

participant "Core Engine\n(Board + Engine)" as Core #LightCoral
participant "useGameBoard\nComposable" as BoardComp #LightYellow
participant "App.vue\nOrchestrator" as App #LightBlue
participant "GameBoard\nComponent" as GameBoard #LightGreen
participant "GenerationCounter\nComponent" as Counter #LightGreen

== Game Loop: Automatic Updates ==

Core -> Core : requestAnimationFrame loop
activate Core
note right
  **Game Loop Steps:**

  1. Check elapsed time vs tickRate
  2. If enough time passed:
     - Calculate next generation
     - Update board state
     - Trigger callback
end note

Core -> Core : calculateNextGeneration()
note right
  Uses RuleSet to evaluate:
  - Living cells (survival)
  - Dead cells with neighbors (birth)
end note

Core -> Core : board.setState(nextCells)
Core -> BoardComp : call updateState() callback
deactivate Core

activate BoardComp
note right of BoardComp
  **updateState callback:**

  Bridge between core logic
  and Vue reactivity system
end note

BoardComp -> BoardComp : livingCells computed updates
BoardComp -> BoardComp : generation ref increments
BoardComp --> App : reactivity triggers
deactivate BoardComp

App -> GameBoard : re-render with new livingCells
App -> Counter : re-render with new generation

note over Core, Counter
  **Performance:**

  requestAnimationFrame ensures:
  - Synced with display refresh
  - Paused when tab inactive
  - Smooth animations

  Only evaluates cells that can change:
  - Living cells (might die)
  - Cells with neighbors (might be born)
end note

@enduml
